From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:14:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: connac: free the pending tokens in an RCU read
 section

mt76_connac2_txwi_free() looks up the station of a frame it isn't given
one for with __mt76_wcid_ptr(), an rcu_dereference(). The tx-free path
calls it inside the rx poll's rcu_read_lock(); mt76_connac2_tx_token_put()
(full reset, unregister) calls it under spin_lock_bh(&dev->token_lock)
only. With BH off that's already a read-side section to RCU, so no
station can be freed under it, but lockdep doesn't count it and reports
suspicious RCU usage, and stops checking locks after its first report.

Take rcu_read_lock() around the loop. On a lockdep kernel
mt76_connac_test_token_put no longer reports it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt76_connac_mac.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt76_connac_mac.c b/mt76_connac_mac.c
index ef71b95f..d0d0f2da 100644
--- a/mt76_connac_mac.c
+++ b/mt76_connac_mac.c
@@ -1301,10 +1301,14 @@ void mt76_connac2_tx_token_put(struct mt76_dev *dev)
 	int id;
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->token_lock);
+	/* txwi_free() looks up each frame's station, as the rx poll's
+	 * tx-free path does in its RCU read section */
+	rcu_read_lock();
 	idr_for_each_entry(&dev->token, txwi, id) {
 		mt76_connac2_txwi_free(dev, txwi, NULL, NULL);
 		dev->token_count--;
 	}
+	rcu_read_unlock();
 	dev->wed_token_count = 0;
 	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->token_lock);
 	idr_destroy(&dev->token);
